# Public website review fixes deployed — 31 October 2026

The later [game-image refresh](WEBSITE_IMAGE_REFRESH_2026_10_31.md) supersedes the serving revision documented below; this record describes the earlier deployment.

The owner authorized deployment of the reviewed candidate to the existing public staging service. The updated website is at [Beat my track](https://bmt-stg-e7a444ab-api-tzgxkrwzva-ew.a.run.app/). It identifies Ville Mannari as developer and explicitly leaves the privacy contact pending.

- The API serves 100% of public traffic from `bmt-stg-e7a444ab-api-web-9f7cd85ce28e`, image `website@sha256:9f7cd85ce28e6b2807ecf05e924acd9cd68560712366e79c064e5cc4f67593d9`.
- The former revision `bmt-stg-e7a444ab-api-web-244328226403` remains available with its pre-existing `website-preview` tag. No schema migration, worker or admin release, runtime configuration change, real account operation or physical-device test was performed.
- The immutable local candidate was based on the former image and changes only nine reviewed package files. The final frozen image passed 39 focused tests. The tagged candidate and public origin each passed 13 direct HTTP checks and 103 GET-only browser/security checks; the browser checks covered four screen widths. No real Google verification or deletion was attempted. [Candidate browser results](evidence/website-review-deployment-2026-10-31/candidate-browser-72tgjoxm/verification.json), [public browser results](evidence/website-review-deployment-2026-10-31/live-browser/verification.json), [successful deployment receipt](evidence/website-review-deployment-2026-10-31/resume-r5el1nfz/deployment.json).
- The first candidate passed HTTP checks, but its browser harness used a string predicate blocked by the site's CSP. The harness was corrected to decode images without unsafe evaluation. No traffic was promoted in that attempt. [Failure record](evidence/website-review-deployment-2026-10-31/candidate-browser-3ummniiu/harness-failure.json).
- The first resume attempt used `--set-tags`, which removed the existing `website-preview` tag. A guard stopped before promotion, the original tag was restored to the former revision, and 100% traffic on that revision was verified. The corrected resume uses additive `--update-tags`; the existing tag was present after final promotion and only the new temporary tag was removed. [Tag restoration record](evidence/website-review-deployment-2026-10-31/resume-1rqteuil/tag-guard-failure.json).

The privacy contact, a public download or updates link, physical-phone acceptance and real-owner Google verification remain open. Staging remains marked non-indexable. During database outages the public-page rate limit is local to each process and replica; it is not a shared global edge limit.
